    {
      "section": "article.story-header",
      "variant": "default",
      "content": {
        "logo": {
          "assetRole": "customer.logo",
          "alt": "Meridian Partners",
          "ref": "/assets/marquee/logo-2.svg"
        },
        "title": "Meridian Partners standardises reporting across eleven regional desks",
        "stats": [
          {
            "value": "11",
            "label": "regional desks on one governed project"
          },
          {
            "value": "4 days",
            "label": "saved on every quarterly close"
          },
          {
            "value": "0",
            "label": "manual reconciliations last quarter"
          }
        ],
        "quote": "Every desk had its own version of assets under management, and reconciling them took a week each quarter. Now one tested definition feeds all eleven desks. The quarterly close has become a short review meeting instead of a week of firefighting, and our analysts finally spend their time on questions clients actually ask. When a number changes, we know exactly why, who approved it and which reports it touches.",
        "name": "Tomas Ekberg",
        "role": "Director of Data Platforms"
      },
      "motion": {
        "pattern": "stroke.draw-on",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "render-final-state"
      },
      "style": {
        "strokeShape": "stroke.s10",
        "strokeGradient": "gradient.01"
      }
    },
    {
      "section": "article.story-body",
      "variant": "default",
      "content": {
        "meta": {
          "logo": {
            "assetRole": "customer.logo",
            "alt": "Meridian Partners",
            "ref": "/assets/marquee/logo-2.svg"
          },
          "facts": [
            {
              "label": "Industry",
              "value": "Asset management"
            },
            {
              "label": "Headquarters",
              "value": "Edinburgh, United Kingdom"
            },
            {
              "label": "Data platform and tools used",
              "value": "Quarry, Lattice, Lattice semantic layer"
            }
          ]
        },
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "h3",
            "text": "Eleven desks, eleven versions of the truth"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Meridian Partners manages investment portfolios for pension funds and foundations through eleven regional desks. Each desk had grown its own reporting over the years, built on shared source data but with its own spreadsheets, scripts and definitions."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "The result was eleven slightly different answers to the same questions. Assets under management, net flows and fee income were calculated in subtly different ways depending on who you asked."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h4",
            "text": "A week lost every quarter"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Every quarter-end, analysts from every desk spent most of a week reconciling their figures before anything could go to clients or the board."
          },
          {
            "kind": "quote",
            "text": "We had very good people spending a week every quarter proving that two spreadsheets agreed with each other. That is not analysis. That is archaeology."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "The work was tedious and risky. Small differences were often explained away rather than fixed, and the same discrepancies came back quarter after quarter, each time requiring someone to remember how they had been resolved before."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h3",
            "text": "One project, shared definitions"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Meridian consolidated desk reporting into a single Lattice project. Core figures were rebuilt once, as tested models and certified metrics, and each desk was given ownership of the parts specific to its region."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "The migration took six months and ran desk by desk, starting with the two largest. Each desk kept producing its old reports until the new figures had matched them for a full month."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h4",
            "text": "Agreeing on the definitions first"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Before writing any SQL, desk heads agreed on written definitions for the twelve most important figures. Where desks genuinely needed different views, the differences were made explicit and named."
          },
          {
            "kind": "ul",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "Twelve core metrics defined once in the semantic layer."
              },
              {
                "text": "Desk-specific views built on top, never alongside."
              },
              {
                "text": "Every metric owned by a named person with a backup."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "h3",
            "text": "Reviews and tests that replace reconciliation"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Every change to a shared model is reviewed by at least one person from another desk. Tests check that regional totals always sum to the firm-wide figure, so a mismatch is caught on the day it happens rather than at quarter-end."
          },
          {
            "kind": "quote",
            "text": "The first quarter-end on the new project was strangely quiet. We kept waiting for the reconciliation to start, and then realised it had been happening every day in the tests."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h4",
            "text": "Lineage for client questions"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "When a client asks how a figure was calculated, analysts can now show the exact models, tests and approvals behind it, generated straight from the project."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Client-facing teams say this has changed the tone of difficult conversations. Instead of promising to look into a figure, they can explain it on the spot, with the evidence in front of them."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h3",
            "text": "Results"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Meridian’s quarterly close is now four days shorter, and there were no manual reconciliations at all last quarter."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h4",
            "text": "More time for clients"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Analysts who used to spend quarter-end reconciling now spend it preparing client commentary, which client relationship managers say has noticeably improved."
          },
          {
            "kind": "quote",
            "text": "Our analysts are writing about markets again instead of about spreadsheets. Clients noticed before we told them anything had changed."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "The firm has also started publishing a short internal note each quarter describing any changes to metric definitions, so that nobody is surprised by a figure that moved for a methodological reason."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h3",
            "text": "Next steps"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Meridian plans to bring its risk reporting into the same project next year and is piloting an assistant for client-facing teams that reads the same certified metrics as every desk."
          },
          {
            "kind": "h4",
            "text": "Expanding to risk"
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Risk models will follow the same pattern: shared definitions, desk ownership and tests that catch disagreements as soon as they appear."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "The team expects risk to be harder than performance reporting, because some of the models involve judgement as well as arithmetic. Writing those judgements down and agreeing who owns them is the first milestone."
          }
        ]
      },
      "motion": {
        "pattern": "static",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "none-needed"
      },
      "style": {
        "chapterLevel": "h3"
      }
    },
    {
      "section": "article.related-stories",
      "variant": "default",
      "content": {
        "eyebrow": "More stories from data teams",
        "title": "Teams that ship trusted data with Lattice",
        "cards": [
          {
            "logo": {
              "assetRole": "customer.logo",
              "alt": "Tidepool",
              "ref": "/assets/marquee/logo-3.svg"
            },
            "title": "Tidepool rebuilt its product analytics on tested models and cut ad hoc requests to the data team by more than two thirds",
